Z||000002||mrfiero||12-20-2001||10:45 PM||||All '84 Indy Fieros and '86-'87 SE's came with the "GT" dual exhaust.  It is a simple bolt on mod from the cat back......you just need to find a GT exhaust system. <P>If you have a basic coupe (other than '88) then you may need to cut a notch in the rear fascia for the passenger side exhaust tips to fit.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Pondski||12-20-2001||11:41 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> -- I have an original "Indy" exhaust that can be welded to your existing "cat" and bolt right up to your engine cradle. It is in perfect condition with no rust. Email me if you are need to know how to do it.<P><P>------------------<BR>Thanks, Chris <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/wbsmileyus.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000004||Jncomutt||12-22-2001||12:51 AM||||I posted pics of mine about a week back.  Its custom designed, its loud.  I'm not sure if its exactly what you'd be looking for, it does use the stock GT tips tho...  Use the search I'm sure it'll come up... Subject was "New exhaust installed"<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fierokid87||12-22-2001||03:40 PM||||I had GT exaust on my 4 cyld when I was still drivng the Fiero as a 4 cyld.  Perfect fit.  Only thing you may want to do is locate the passenger side tial pipe hanger.<P>Scott<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="red"> Fierokid's  Web site:</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="white">http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero</FONT><P><FONT COLOR="blue">AIM: Fierokid87<BR>ICQ: Fierokid</FONT><P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierokid.gif"> ||||reg||1
